// Unreal-side entry file for the BrickPack kernels (ray-marching plan P1-B).
//
// This file deliberately contains NO logic. It exists because Unreal compiles
// a shader by (virtual file path, entry point name), and because the kernels
// themselves live outside the Unreal project — in voxel-core/shaders, which is
// engine-free, so the same text can be compiled by an offline DXC leg and by a
// future standalone bench without an engine in the loop.
//
// It is the VoxelWorldGen.usf pattern, with one difference worth stating:
// brickpack.ush carries NO worldgen version lock, because it contains no
// worldgen math — only the Cells layout convention. So the shader classes for
// BrickClassifyMain and BrickPackMain must NOT derive from FVoxelWorldGenShader
// (which passes VXC_WORLDGEN_VERSION_CPP in); they need VXC_UE and nothing else.
// The argument is VoxelAssetStamp.usf's, and its header has the long version.
//
// Platform.ush must come first — it defines the per-platform intrinsics and
// type plumbing every Unreal shader is compiled against.
//
// VXC_UE switches brickpack.ush's resource DECLARATIONS (not its arithmetic)
// over to Unreal's conventions: no explicit register() slots, and the parameter
// fields declared as loose globals so they land in $Globals where Unreal's
// shader parameter struct binds them by reflected name.

#include "/Engine/Public/Platform.ush"
#include "/VoxelCore/brickpack.ush"
